<title>RUSSIA: Rouble eases on central bank, T-bill selling.</title>
<headline>Rouble eases on central bank, T-bill selling.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rouble eased on Wednesday after selling on Tuesday by commercial banks, dealers said, adding that moves by traditional Treasury bill investors moving into dollars were pressing the rouble.</p>
<p> roubles/dollar	Feb 19 midday  Feb 19 early   Feb 18 close</p>
<p> today settlement    5,661-63	 5,659-61	 5,649-51</p>
<p> tomorrow settlement 5,664-65	 5,660-62	 5,658-59</p>
<p> overnight credit (%)   20-25	    20-25	     5-10</p>
<p>			   Feb 19				Feb 18</p>
<p> central bank	  5,654/70			    5,653/67</p>
<p> MICEX		   5,662				 5,659</p>
<p>&quot;Interest in T-bill investments is going down (due to lowering yields) and dollar buying has been seen since yesterday,&quot; Bank Menatep dealer Mikhail Zaretsky said.</p>
<p>But he added the rouble was firming during in speculative trading and on bank client buying.</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
